40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 6 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(SYSTEMS DESIGN) Tj
T*
(The City of Gladstone shall provide the Gladstone Fire Department an Advanced Life) Tj
T*
(Support \(ALS\) ambulance service. This service shall be ordered on calls for service within) Tj
T*
(the City of Gladstone, as well requests from outside agencies for mutual aid. This service) Tj
T*
(shall provide for a timely response, quality patient care and patient transports to an) Tj
T*
(appropriate medical facility. In the event the fire department is unable to respond, a) Tj
T*
(mutual aid provider shall be requested.) Tj
T*
(Non-emergency response shall include but not necessarily limited to the following:) Tj
T*
(1. Scheduled direct admissions to a hospital.) Tj
T*
(2. Hospital to home transfers, or nursing home to extended care facility transfers.) Tj
T*
(3. Home to hospital for medical tests.) Tj
T*
(Emergency responses shall include but not limited to the following:) Tj
T*
(1. Any call involving trauma resulting from an accident, fall, sports injury, burn, or etc.,) Tj
T*
(incident that results in injury requiring immediate medical attention.) Tj
T*
(2. Any call involving an illness resulting from diabetes, heart condition, strokes,) Tj
T*
(seizures, or etc., any serious illness requiring immediate medical attention.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
