T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 7 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/25/2025) Tj
T*
(MEDICAL CONTROL FORMAT) Tj
T*
(All patient treatment and transport shall follow guidelines as listed in current protocol.) Tj
T*
(Medical Control shall be contacted when indicated in the individual protocol, or when any) Tj
T*
(problem or question exists. This is to ensure quality patient care on-scene, enroute to and) Tj
T*
(upon arrival at the destination hospital.) Tj
T*
(When transporting a patient to a hospital other than the medical control hospital and orders) Tj
T*
(are to be requested, the "other" receiving hospital should be contacted directly.) Tj
T*
(The following information should be transmitted to the medical control hospital in all) Tj
T*
(emergency situations:) Tj
T*
(1. Paramedic's name and unit/service.) Tj
T*
(2. Expected arrival time.) Tj
T*
(3. Patient's chief complaint and brief history.) Tj
T*
(4. Patient's condition \(including GCS\).) Tj
T*
(5. Patient's vital signs.) Tj
T*
(6. Findings of exam and treatment.) Tj
T*
(7. Request for additional orders or questions.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
