stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 9 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(DRUG ACCOUNTABILITY) Tj
T*
(The purpose of this protocol is to provide guidelines for the security, inventory and record) Tj
T*
(keeping procedures for all scheduled narcotic medications in accordance with Fire / EMS) Tj
T*
(Division policy F458 - Schedule Drug.) Tj
T*
(1. The following are considered scheduled narcotic drugs requiring strict) Tj
T*
(accountability:) Tj
T*
(A. Morphine Sulfate) Tj
T*
(B. Versed - 2mg vials) Tj
T*
(C. Versed - 5mg vials - Nasal) Tj
T*
(D. Fentanyl - 100 mcg vials) Tj
T*
(E. Ketamine - 500mg vials) Tj
T*
(2. The drugs listed above shall be kept in the following manner:) Tj
T*
(A. Limited quantities shall be maintained in a sealed/tagged tamper) Tj
T*
(proof container. This container shall be stored inside the Narcotic Safe) Tj
T*
(located within the patient compartment of the ambulance.) Tj
T*
(B. The following shall be considered minimum quantities to be carried in) Tj
T*
(the ambulance at all times. Supply shall be restocked as soon as possible.) Tj
T*
(1. 4 Morphine Sulfate) Tj
T*
(2. 4 Versed 2mg) Tj
T*
(3. 4 Versed 5mg - Nasal) Tj
T*
(4. 4 Fentanyl - 100mcg) Tj
T*
(5. 2 Ketamine vials - 500mg) Tj
T*
(3. Daily inventory and drug accountability shall be the responsibility of the off-going) Tj
T*
(and on-coming paramedic. Inventory and accountability shall be completed) Tj
T*
(in the following manner:) Tj
T*
(A. At the beginning of each shift the off going and the on coming) Tj
T*
(paramedics shall conduct a joint inventory of the scheduled drugs on the) Tj
T*
(ambulance.) Tj
T*
(B. As the inventory is completed, each paramedic shall sign the logbook.) Tj
T*
(This log shall contain the following:) Tj
T*
(1. Date and time) Tj
T*
(2. Quantity of drug) Tj
T*
(3. Lock identification #) Tj
T*
(4. Paramedics' signatures and employee #) Tj
T*
(C. The inventory procedure shall be completed at any time there is a change) Tj
T*
(in the on duty paramedic regardless of the time of day.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
