stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 10 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(D. On the 1st day of every month in the presence of an authorized officer the on) Tj
T*
(duty paramedic shall open the sealed/tagged narcotic box and perform a) Tj
T*
(physical inventory; also inspecting for signs of tampering and expired) Tj
T*
(narcotics \(see below\). The unit container shall be restocked / resealed and) Tj
T*
(documented in the logbook accordingly.) Tj
T*
(Broken Seal Procedure:) Tj
T*
(A. If a seal is found to be broken, the paramedic is to immediately notify a) Tj
T*
(supervisor.) Tj
T*
(B. The supervisor and paramedic will together conduct an audit of the narcotics) Tj
T*
(box and verify the contents.) Tj
T*
(C. The supervisor will make an entry in the narcotic log to document the broken) Tj
T*
(seal; both the supervisor and medic will sign the log.) Tj
T*
(D. The supervisor will draft a memo to the Fire Chief going through the Chain of) Tj
T*
(Command for his/her shift.\(CC Narcotics Officer\) explaining the incident.) Tj
T*
(E. At the discretion of the Fire Chief, a sample of a narcotic\(s\) may be sent to the) Tj
T*
(Missouri State Highway Patrol lab for content verification.) Tj
T*
(Expired Medication Procedure) Tj
T*
(A. In the event expired narcotics are found during off hours, they shall be taped and) Tj
T*
(marked as "expired do not use" placed back in the tagged narcotic container until) Tj
T*
(they can be placed into the Supply Safe expired inventory.) Tj
T*
(B. In the presence of an authorized officer the expired narcotics will be removed and) Tj
T*
(deducted from the ambulance inventory and noted as placed into the expired) Tj
T*
(inventory.) Tj
T*
(C. The ambulance inventory shall then be restocked, re-tagged and logged, a piece) Tj
T*
(of tape will be placed on the outside of the container with the name of the) Tj
T*
(medications and expiration dates clearly listed.) Tj
T*
(D. Expired narcotics will then be placed into the expired container located in the) Tj
T*
(Supply Safe and logged in the "Expired Narcotics Log," this is located in the back) Tj
T*
(of the Supply Safe log. The expired container shall be re-tagged, logged and resecured.) Tj
T*
(4. Drug administration records shall be maintained on all scheduled drugs. These) Tj
T*
(records shall be completed at the time of care and shall indicate the following:) Tj
T*
(A. Date and time of administration.) Tj
T*
(B. Name of patient.) Tj
T*
(C. Physician giving order for administration if applicable.) Tj
T*
(D. Quantity administered.) Tj
T*
(E. Paramedic's signature.) Tj
T*
(F. All unused portions shall be discarded at the hospital prior to returning to) Tj
T*
(service. The amount discarded and the signature of the witness must be on) Tj
T*
(the usage form. It is preferred HOSPITAL STAFF WITNESS DISPOSAL, If) Tj
T*
(not possible have a supervisor witness.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
