stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 11 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(HELICOPTER UTILIZATION) Tj
T*
(1. Indications) Tj
T*
(A. Need for optimum speed of response and transport. \(Keep in mind helicopter) Tj
T*
(response and loading time\).) Tj
T*
(B. Impaired ground accessibility due to location, traffic or condition of roads.) Tj
T*
(C. Shortage of ground transport units and there is a need for rapid transit.) Tj
T*
(D. Need to achieve distribution of patients among area hospitals. \(Mass casualty) Tj
T*
(Incident\).) Tj
T*
(2. Procedures) Tj
T*
(A. It is the responsibility of the attending Paramedic and the Incident) Tj
T*
(Commander to assess the situation and determine the need for air ambulance) Tj
T*
(transport.) Tj
T*
(B. If an air ambulance is needed it is the responsibility of the Incident) Tj
T*
(Commander to contact dispatch and request it.) Tj
T*
(C. It shall be the responsibility of the Incident Commander or designee along with) Tj
T*
(law enforcement to establish a suitable landing site. This site should be:) Tj
T*
(1. 100 feet square.) Tj
T*
(2. Free of overhead obstructions.) Tj
T*
(3. Accessible to aircraft for patient transfer.) Tj
T*
(4. A fire apparatus with foam application capabilities should be available.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
