stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 12 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(08/05/2026) Tj
T*
(PATIENT DESTINATION CRITERIA) Tj
T*
(1. General) Tj
T*
(A. For all life-threatening emergencies transport the patient to the nearest) Tj
T*
(appropriate facility.) Tj
T*
(B. When the nearest appropriate facility conflicts with the choice of the) Tj
T*
(patient or a person acting in the behalf of the patient, contact Medical) Tj
T*
(Control.) Tj
T*
(C. For all non-life-threatening emergencies, transport may be made to the) Tj
T*
(following facilities: North Kansas City Hospital, St. Luke's Northland, Liberty) Tj
T*
(Hospital, Truman/Truman West, Veterans Medical Center- Kansas City, St.) Tj
T*
(Luke's-Plaza, K.U. Medical Center, and Research.) Tj
T*
(2. Trauma Criteria) Tj
T*
(A. Any trauma patient meeting the following criteria should be considered for) Tj
T*
(transport to a Level I/II trauma center \(NKCH, Liberty, KUMC or) Tj
T*
(Truman\)\(Children's Mercy Hospital for patients under the age of 18\) even if not) Tj
T*
(the nearest facility, a high index of suspicion should be maintained regardless) Tj
T*
(of time lapsed from point of injury to EMS patient contact:) Tj
T*
(Trauma Activation) Tj
T*
(-Trauma code) Tj
T*
(-GCS < 8 with MOI or other signs of shock.) Tj
T*
(-Confirmed & sustained systolic BP <90 & age specific for) Tj
T*
(pediatrics.) Tj
T*
(-Respiratory compromise/obstruction and/or intubation Resp rate >29 or <10.) Tj
T*
(-GSW to head, neck, or torso.) Tj
T*
(-BP <90, Absent peripheral pulses.) Tj
T*
(-Fall with head injury of patient taking anticoagulants.) Tj
T*
(Trauma Alert) Tj
T*
(-Confirmed active hemorrhage) Tj
T*
(-GCS <14) Tj
T*
(-Extremity trauma with loss of distal pulse of sensation.) Tj
T*
(-MVC with:) Tj
T*
(Major auto deformity >1 foot) Tj
T*
(Unrestrained rollover) Tj
T*
(Death in same passenger compartment) Tj
T*
(Extrication >20 minutes) Tj
T*
(Ejection from vehicle) Tj
T*
(-MCC or ATV crash >20 mph or separation of rider from vehicle.) Tj
T*
(-Auto vs. pedestrian/bicycle) Tj
T*
(-Penetrating injury \(i.e. stab wound\) to head, neck, or torso.) Tj
T*
(-Major burns >20% BSA or involving inhalation injury.) Tj
T*
(-Falls > 3 feet.) Tj
T*
(-Pelvic fractures) Tj
T*
(-Open fractures) Tj
T*
(-Pregnant trauma patients >20 weeks gestation) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
