stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 15 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/25/2025) Tj
T*
(PRE-HOSPITAL DEATH DETERMINATION) Tj
T*
(Patients who have obviously expired will not be resuscitated or transported by Gladstone) Tj
T*
(EMS personnel if any of the following obvious signs of death are present:) Tj
T*
(Trauma Related) Tj
T*
(A. If there is any doubt the arrest state is traumatic or any question concerning any sign) Tj
T*
(of life at the scene, then resuscitation should be initiated and Medical Control) Tj
T*
(contacted.) Tj
T*
(B. A patient with obvious traumatic injuries not consistent with human life, for example) Tj
T*
(decapitation, incineration, transection of thorax \(hemicorpectomy\), massive trauma) Tj
T*
(with visible organ damage; who is asystolic \(confirmed in three leads\) or has no) Tj
T*
(audible heart sounds and who has not been observed at the scene to possess any) Tj
T*
(sign of life \(verbal or motor response, respiratory effort, or palpable pulse\) may be) Tj
T*
(pronounced DOA.) Tj
T*
(C. If unable to begin CPR in a reasonable amount of time due to patient accessibility or) Tj
T*
(location, contact Medical Control and notify them of patient's condition and) Tj
T*
(circumstances that prohibit appropriate resuscitation.) Tj
T*
(D. Documentation of any of the above findings shall occur in the ambulance run report.) Tj
T*
(Medical Related) Tj
T*
(A. A patient in cardiopulmonary arrest due to medical causes may be pronounced DOA) Tj
T*
(if they are asystolic \(confirmed in three leads\) or have no audible heart sounds and) Tj
T*
(also have one of the following signs:) Tj
T*
(1. Rigor mortis) Tj
T*
(2. Dependent lividity) Tj
T*
(3. Decomposition) Tj
T*
(B. Rigor mortis and asystole are not reliable signs of death in the hypothermic. If) Tj
T*
(hypothermia is a consideration, resuscitation should be initiated.) Tj
T*
(C. Generalized tissue decomposition is not compatible with life; the patient may be) Tj
T*
(pronounced DOA without cardiac monitor application.) Tj
T*
(D. If rigor mortis, lividity, or tissue decomposition is present, medical control) Tj
T*
(contact is not necessary.) Tj
T*
(E. Any of the above findings shall be documented in the ambulance run report.) Tj
T*
(For all emergency scenes where patient needs exceed available EMS resources, initial) Tj
T*
(assessment and treatment shall be in accordance with an approved triage methodology.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
