stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 16 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(REPORT WRITING) Tj
T*
(Documentation is one of the most important tasks that we perform as pre-hospital providers.) Tj
T*
(While there are many reasons to document, the main purpose of documentation is to) Tj
T*
(provide an accurate, comprehensive, and permanent record of each patient's condition and) Tj
T*
(the treatment rendered. Always remember if it's not written down it didn't happen.) Tj
T*
(Any pertinent notes and information should be left with the receiving hospital. This) Tj
T*
(would include any cardiac strips in cases of a STEMI. Signatures from the receiving) Tj
T*
(hospital whould be captured electronically on currenty RMS System. The formal EMS) Tj
T*
(report shall be completed prior to the end of shift.) Tj
T*
(Listed below is the minimum criterion required for Gladstone EMS reports.) Tj
T*
(A. How the call was received from dispatch, pre-arrival information, units responding) Tj
T*
(location and mode of response.) Tj
T*
(B. Nature of the call on arrival.) Tj
T*
(C. How the patient was found, presenting signs, appearance and pertinent scene) Tj
T*
(factors.) Tj
T*
(D. The patient's chief complaint.) Tj
T*
(E. HPI & PPMH) Tj
T*
(F. Two sets of vital signs. This includes: blood pressure, pulse rate, respiratory rate, and) Tj
T*
(SpO2 and EtCO2 readings if applicable.) Tj
T*
(G. IV attempts, location, patency and who initiates.) Tj
T*
(H. Intubation attempts, ET tube location measured from the teeth in cm, and) Tj
T*
(confirmation methods.) Tj
T*
(I. Medication administration, name, dose, route and results.) Tj
T*
(J. Procedures performed, by whom and results.) Tj
T*
(K. The patient's overall response to treatment and transport.) Tj
T*
(L. Orders requested/received, and given by whom.) Tj
T*
(M. Attending Paramedic shall end the report with their full name, title and state license) Tj
T*
(number \(P#\).) Tj
T*
(All calls shall be documented in the first person, past tense and in chronological) Tj
T*
(order, from the time of dispatch through return to service.) Tj
T*
(All reports shall be written utilizing proper grammar, spelling and only Department) Tj
T*
(approved abbreviations.) Tj
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
