/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 20 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(PRE-HOSPITAL TERMINATION OF RESUSCITATION) Tj
T*
(Numerous studies have proven that a certain population of cardiac arrest patients will not) Tj
T*
(survive hospital discharge if they fail pre-hospital therapy. Patients that meet the) Tj
T*
(criteria) Tj
T*
(below shall be eligible for termination of resuscitative efforts in the field and do not) Tj
T*
(require) Tj
T*
(transport to an Emergency Department. If there is any doubt, continue resuscitative efforts) Tj
T*
(and transport.) Tj
T*
(Inclusion Criteria) Tj
T*
(A. Primary cardiac arrest.) Tj
T*
(B. Age >21 years of age.) Tj
T*
(C. Either asystole or PEA as presenting rhythm.) Tj
T*
(D. Asystole must be the terminal rhythm.) Tj
T*
(E. ETT intubation.) Tj
T*
(F. IV or IO access.) Tj
T*
(G. > 20 minutes of appropriate therapy.) Tj
T*
(H. Capnography reading less than 10 mm/Hg) Tj
T*
(Exclusion Criteria) Tj
T*
(A. Non-primary cardiac arrest \(cause of arrest possibly attributed to other) Tj
T*
(pathology\). Including but not limited to the following:) Tj
T*
(1. Hypothermia) Tj
T*
(2. Drug overdose \(possible acute overdose\).) Tj
T*
(3. Primary respiratory arrest \(i.e. status asthmaticus\).) Tj
T*
(4. Carbon monoxide poisoning) Tj
T*
(5. Traumatic arrest.) Tj
T*
(6. Drowning) Tj
T*
(B. Ventricular fibrillation or ventricular tachycardia at any time during resuscitation.) Tj
T*
(C. Any return of spontaneous circulation during resuscitation.) Tj
T*
(D. Any neurologic activity.) Tj
T*
(E. Family desires transport \(either voiced or perceived\).) Tj
T*
(F. Other, such as unstable scene or disagreement among family members.) Tj
T*
(G. EMS responder witnessed cardiac arrest.) Tj
T*
(Procedure) Tj
T*
(A. Follow appropriate cardiac arrest protocol to include:) Tj
T*
(1. Successful early intubation.) Tj
T*
(2. Successful early IV drug therapy.) Tj
T*
(3. Minimum of 20 minutes of appropriate therapy.) Tj
T*
(B. If the patient fits the inclusion criteria and does not fit any exclusion criteria and) Tj
T*
(the above procedures have been accomplished the paramedic may initiate the) Tj
T*
(termination of resuscitation.) Tj
T*
(C. Paramedic does not need to contact medical control if all criteria is) Tj
T*
(followed.) Tj
T*
(D. The appropriate law enforcement agency must be notified.) Tj
T*
(E. Rhythm strips must accompany report and report must contain the all proper) Tj
T*
(documentation.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
