T*
(PHYSICIAN ON SCENE) Tj
T*
(If a physician is found in attendance of a patient at the scene \(excluding a physicians) Tj
T*
(office\),) Tj
T*
(or a physician comes to the scene after the paramedic has initiated treatment, the) Tj
T*
(paramedic will:) Tj
T*
(A. Advise the physician of your treatment, medical protocols, and additional) Tj
T*
(directives received from Medical Control while continuing patient care.) Tj
T*
(B. If a physician on scene desires to give medical direction regarding the patient care, the) Tj
T*
(paramedic is to explain to the physician that you are functioning under strict medical) Tj
T*
(control protocols. In order for the physician to assume patient care, the physician must) Tj
T*
(be willing to assume full responsibility and liability for the patient. This includes) Tj
T*
(accompanying the patient to the hospital. Medical Control must be contacted) Tj
T*
(immediately and made aware of the situation. Ultimate determination of physician) Tj
T*
(shall be made through Medical Control.) Tj
T*
(C. If a physician in their office is treating a patient and orders are given, they shall be) Tj
T*
(relayed) Tj
T*
(to Medical Control. If a conflict in orders should arise, Medical Control shall overrule all) Tj
T*
(other orders.) Tj
T*
ET
