T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 24 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(ADULT/CHILD ABUSE REPORTING) Tj
T*
(Includes physical abuse, emotional abuse, sexual abuse, or neglect.) Tj
T*
(Duty to Report) Tj
T*
(Any person having reasonable cause to suspect that any child, a handicapped person, or) Tj
T*
(elderly adult has been or may be abused or neglected shall make a report to the appropriate) Tj
T*
(law enforcement agency and contact the following agencies:) Tj
T*
(Missouri Child Abuse Hotline - 1-800-392-3738) Tj
T*
(Missouri Adult Abuse Hotline - 1-800-392-0210) Tj
T*
(Assessment/Treatment) Tj
T*
(A. Provide necessary medical care according to the appropriate protocol.) Tj
T*
(B. Although a preliminary assessment of abuse or neglect is made in the field,) Tj
T*
(appropriate personnel make the final determination upon review of the incident.) Tj
T*
(Accusations of abuse or neglect should not be made in the field.) Tj
T*
(Notification) Tj
T*
(A. In a private and confidential environment notify the physician at the receiving hospital) Tj
T*
(of the facts upon which neglect of abuse is suspected.) Tj
T*
(B. Notification of the shift supervisor of the facts of the neglect or abuse is encouraged.) Tj
T*
(Documentation) Tj
T*
(A. The following information shall be included in the attending paramedics report:) Tj
T*
(1. All facts upon which abuse or neglect is suspected.) Tj
T*
(2. Identity of physician notified.) Tj
T*
(3. Whether physician or hospital staff is going to make proper notification.) Tj
T*
(4. If notification is made by the attending paramedic.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
