(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(PARENT-CHILD CONSIDERATIONS) Tj
T*
(A. In general, a parent should accompany most conscious children during transport) Tj
T*
(unless the parent's presence interferes with the care of the child.) Tj
T*
(B. In situations of major trauma and cardiopulmonary arrest the paramedic should) Tj
T*
(exercise his or her judgment as to the status of the parent riding in the ambulance.) Tj
T*
(C. Allow the parent to hold and touch the child whenever possible.) Tj
T*
(D. Both the parent and child respond best to open and honest dialogue.) Tj
T*
ET
