(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 26 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(Do-Not-Resuscitate / Advanced Directives / Emergency Order) Tj
T*
(Sets) Tj
T*
(Missouri law provides for the observance of: Advance Directives, Do-Not-Resuscitate orders) Tj
T*
(and) Tj
T*
(Emergency Order Sets when executed in compliance with Missouri state statute.) Tj
T*
(Advanced Directives) Tj
T*
(The Advanced Directive becomes effective only when the declarant's condition is terminal and) Tj
T*
(the) Tj
T*
(declarant does not have the capacity to make health-care decisions. Sec. 459.025, RSMo. It) Tj
T*
(is) Tj
T*
(designed to allow a patient to forgo "death prolonging procedures," which are defined as) Tj
T*
("any) Tj
T*
(medical procedure or intervention which, when applied to a patient, would serve only to) Tj
T*
(prolong the) Tj
T*
(dying process and where, in the judgment of the attending physician pursuant to usual and) Tj
T*
(customary medical standards, death will occur within a short time whether or not such) Tj
T*
(procedure or) Tj
T*
(intervention is utilized. Death-prolonging procedures shall not include the administration) Tj
T*
(of) Tj
T*
(medication or the performance of medical procedures deemed necessary to provide comfort,) Tj
T*
(care) Tj
T*
(or to alleviate pain nor the performance of any procedure to provide nutrition or) Tj
T*
(hydration." Sec.) Tj
T*
(459.010\(3\), RSMo.) Tj
T*
(Transportable Physician Orders for Patient Preferences \(TPOPP\)) Tj
T*
(The Transportable Physician Orders for Patient Preferences \(TPOPP\) aims to improve the) Tj
T*
(communication of a person's preferences regarding life-sustaining treatments and, thereby,) Tj
T*
(generate high quality medical care in accordance with Sec. 459.010\(3\), RSMo. In order to) Tj
T*
(accomplish this aim, TPOPP was designed to:) Tj
T*
(* Document a person's treatment preferences regarding CPR and the use of) Tj
T*
(mechanical intervention for breathing/ventilation along with other life-sustaining) Tj
T*
(treatments such as tube feedings, etc.) Tj
T*
(* Translate those preferences into an actionable portable set of physician orders) Tj
T*
(* Communicate an individual's care preferences across health settings) Tj
T*
(* Reduce repetitive documentation while complying with state laws and the) Tj
T*
(Federal Patient Self-Determination Act.) Tj
T*
(When properly executed in accordance with Sec. 459.025, RSMo, the TPOPP shall be accepted) Tj
T*
(and honored by the attending paramedic.) Tj
T*
(Do-Not-Resuscitate \(DNR\)) Tj
T*
(Outside the hospital "Do-Not-Resuscitate" \(DNR\) requests are orders provided by a patient's) Tj
T*
(physician to refrain from initiating cardiopulmonary resuscitative measures in the event of) Tj
T*
(a cardiac) Tj
T*
(or respiratory arrest. DNR requests are compatible with maximal therapeutic care and the) Tj
T*
(patient) Tj
T*
(may receive vigorous support \(i.e. IV's & drugs\) until the point of cardiac or respiratory) Tj
T*
(arrest.) Tj
T*
(Outside the hospital "Do-Not-Resuscitate" orders, are regulated by RSMo sections 190.600 to) Tj
T*
(190.621. When properly executed, the DNR shall be accepted and honored by the attending) Tj
T*
(paramedic. Missouri Bureau of EMS has ruled a photocopy / fax is also acceptable. DNR FAQ's) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
