T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(Guidelines) Tj
T*
(Guidelines for acceptance of a DNR request include:) Tj
T*
(A. If any doubt exists about the validity of the DNR form or the intent of the patient or) Tj
T*
(the) Tj
T*
(appropriate surrogate, resuscitation must be initiated and Medical Control contacted.) Tj
T*
(B. Only the approved Bureau of EMS DNR form \(MO580-1936\) shall be used.) Tj
T*
(C. The DNR form must be signed and dated by the patient or appropriate surrogate, a witness,) Tj
T*
(and the patient's physician.) Tj
T*
(D. The revocation provision must remain unsigned in order for this DNR form to remain valid.) Tj
T*
(E. The DNR form must be with the patient at the time of the EMS providers' arrival.) Tj
T*
(F. The EMS provider must see the form.) Tj
T*
(G. No cardiac monitoring is necessary. No Medical Control contact is necessary.) Tj
T*
(H. If this form is presented after care has begun, all resuscitative efforts shall cease and) Tj
T*
(Medical Control shall be notified.) Tj
T*
(Documentation) Tj
T*
(The EMS report shall include the existence of a \(DNR, DPA, TPOPP or other forms of Advanced) Tj
T*
(Directives\). A copy shall be attached to the EMS report. The original form shall remain at) Tj
T*
(the) Tj
T*
(facility or home. If the patient is transported, the form\(s\) will accompany the patient.) Tj
T*
(Emergency Order Sets) Tj
T*
(Pediatric Emergency Form) Tj
T*
(Children's Mercy Hospital \(CMH\) has developed a form for special medical needs pediatric) Tj
T*
(patients) Tj
T*
(who require very specific emergency medical care.) Tj
T*
(Upon arrival of EMS providers, the parent / caregiver shall provide a "Pediatric Emergency) Tj
T*
(Form" to) Tj
T*
(EMS personnel, which contains detailed emergency instructions, medical history and hospital) Tj
T*
(emergency contact information. The Pediatric Emergency Form shall supercede existing) Tj
T*
(protocol and shall be followed by the attending paramedic.) Tj
T*
(If questions arise regarding the specific orders listed on the form, Children's Mercy) Tj
T*
(Hospital can be) Tj
T*
(contacted at the phone numbers listed on the Pediatric Emergency Form. When contacted, the) Tj
T*
(attending paramedic shall provide the hospital with the Medical Record \(MR\) number listed on) Tj
T*
(the) Tj
T*
(top right corner of the form. Children's Mercy Hospital personnel will utilize the MR number) Tj
T*
(to) Tj
T*
(confirm the specific orders.) Tj
T*
(In addition, CMH has advised parents / caregivers to have a "File of Life" information card) Tj
T*
(located) Tj
T*
(on the refrigerator in the patients' residence.) Tj
T*
(Documentation) Tj
T*
(The EMS report shall include the existence of a "Pediatric Emergency Form." A copy shall be) Tj
T*
(attached to the EMS report. The original form\(s\) shall be transported with the patient and) Tj
T*
(given to) Tj
T*
(CMH staff.) Tj
T*
ET
