T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(PATIENT REFUSALS) Tj
T*
(Purpose) Tj
T*
(To establish guidelines and authorization for allowing a patient to refuse procedures,) Tj
T*
(treatment and or transport.) Tj
T*
(Procedure) Tj
T*
(The paramedic will be allowed to accept patient refusals provided sufficient information) Tj
T*
(about the patient's condition have been given, allowing the patient or responsible person to) Tj
T*
(make an informed decision, and:) Tj
T*
(1. Patient is a mentally competent adult, 18 years of age or older.) Tj
T*
(2. If the patient is not mentally competent, an authorized caregiver with power of attorney) Tj
T*
(or) Tj
T*
(guardianship may refuse in lieu of.) Tj
T*
(3. If the patient is under the age of 18, a parent or guardian must sign the refusal unless:) Tj
T*
(a. The minor is emancipated) Tj
T*
(b. Married) Tj
T*
(c. Pregnant) Tj
T*
