(ADVANCE BENEFICIARY NOTICE) Tj
T*
(Purpose) Tj
T*
(To establish a guideline for the use of the Advanced Beneficiary Notice \(ABN\).) Tj
T*
(Procedure) Tj
T*
(1. Medicare requires the Advanced Beneficiary Notice \(ABN\) when it is likely that costs for) Tj
T*
(treatment and transport will not be covered.) Tj
T*
(2. The form is designed to help patients make an informed choice about whether or not to) Tj
T*
(receive services, knowing that services may not be covered.) Tj
T*
(2. The form is to be filled out for all Medicare and Blue Cross insured patients.) Tj
T*
(3. The form is not intended to discourage treatment and/or transport; it is to help patients) Tj
T*
(make an informed decision.) Tj
T*
(4. The attending paramedic shall inform Medicare and Blue Cross patients when it is) Tj
T*
(possible that services will not be covered. The patient shall be given the form to read,) Tj
T*
(check yes, services are wanted, or no, services are not desired. The form is to be) Tj
T*
(signed and dated by the patient or a person acting on behalf of the patient.) Tj
T*
(5. Should the patient refuse to sign, date it and mark the form refused to sign.) Tj
T*
(6. The completed form shall be attached to the hospital face sheet and forwarded to the) Tj
T*
(City billing clerk.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
