T*
(1. Open airway and assess for breathing.) Tj
T*
(2. If no breathing present follow AHA guidelines for obstructed airway. Attempt ventilation.) Tj
T*
(3. If unsuccessful, use direct laryngoscopy to check for foreign bodies. If present, remove) Tj
T*
(with magill) Tj
T*
(forceps. Assist ventilations as needed.) Tj
T*
(4. If still unsuccessful, consider surgical cricothyrotomy airway or commercial) Tj
T*
(cricothyrotomy device. All) Tj
T*
(other airway techniques must be attempted prior to surgical airway.) Tj
T*
(5. If resolved or initially only partially obstructed, do the following:) Tj
T*
(a. Transport in upright position.) Tj
T*
(b. Administer O2.) Tj
T*
(c. Establish IV access.) Tj
T*
(d. Monitor respiratory status.) Tj
T*
(Asthma) Tj
T*
(1. Ensure airway.) Tj
T*
(2. Establish IV access.) Tj
T*
(3. Administer O2 using appropriate administration set, for Status Asthmaticus consider early) Tj
T*
(CPAP with inline breathing treatment. Intubation should be considered in patients exhibiting) Tj
T*
(signs of physical exhaustion/respiratory failure. If the patient is conscious and needs to) Tj
T*
(be) Tj
