(7/25/2023) Tj
T*
(CONGESTIVE HEART FAILURE \(CHF\)) Tj
T*
(1. Ensure airway.) Tj
T*
(2. Rapid CPAP for severe respiratory distress; Administer O2 and assist ventilations as) Tj
T*
(needed. Intubation should be considered in patients exhibiting signs of physical) Tj
T*
(exhaustion/respiratory failure. If the patient is conscious and needs to be intubated,) Tj
T*
(consider Versed 2-4 mg SIVP up to a total dose of 10mg. If unable to obtain IV access,) Tj
T*
(consider IN Versed 2-4 mg, max 10 mg. See intranasal procedure.) Tj
T*
(3. Monitor cardiac rhythm and obtain 12/15 lead ECG.) Tj
T*
(4. Start an IV at a TKO rate. Carefully monitor fluid.) Tj
T*
(5. Nitroglycerin 0.4mg SL if the patient maintains a systolic blood pressure > 100, and a) Tj
T*
(pulse rate >50 and <140. May be repeated every 5 minutes until distress is relieved, or) Tj
T*
(systolic blood pressure < 100, or 3 doses.) Tj
T*
(6. If EtCO2 indicates constrictive pattern you may consider Duoneb 3 ml nebulized. Set) Tj
T*
(O2 at 6-8 Lpm. Consider if needed Albuterol 2.5mg x 2, heart rate should not exceeds) Tj
T*
(150 bpm. Xoponex may also be considered if other medications are ineffective or) Tj
T*
(contraindicated.) Tj
T*
ET
