(CVA/STROKES) Tj
T*
(Consider stroke in any patient presenting with the following:) Tj
T*
(- Altered mental status) Tj
T*
(- Dysarthria \(slurred speech\)) Tj
T*
(- Aphasia \(difficulty understanding or expressing speech\)) Tj
T*
(- Weakness or Numbness in the face, arm, or leg) Tj
T*
(- Vision \(blurry vision, double vision, Blindness\)) Tj
T*
(- Dizziness, loss of balance, loss of coordination) Tj
T*
(- Headache \(especially if sudden or severe\)) Tj
T*
(Assessment) Tj
T*
(1. Check vital signs) Tj
T*
(2. Briefly assess pulmonary, cardiac, and neurological systems.) Tj
T*
(3. Determine time patient was last known normal) Tj
T*
(4. Administer Cincinnati Stroke Scale) Tj
T*
(5. Administer VAN Score) Tj
T*
(6. Determine Blood Glucose Level) Tj
T*
(7. Other specific history of importance includes) Tj
T*
(a. medications \(especially anticoagulants\),) Tj
T*
(b. recent surgeries \(3 month brain or spine, 21 days major surgeries\)) Tj
T*
(c. history of brain tumor or aneurysm, history of bleeding disorders.) Tj
T*
(Treatment) Tj
T*
(1. Administer 02 as appropriate to maintain O2 saturation >94%) Tj
T*
(2. Place on Cardiac Monitor and pulse oximeter) Tj
T*
(3. Start an IV TKO) Tj
T*
(4. Treat blood glucose per protocol) Tj
T*
ET
