T*
(HYPER-AGITATED DELIRIUM SYNDROME) Tj
T*
(The purpose of this protocol is to identify and treat those patients experiencing) Tj
T*
(Hyper-Agitated Delirium by mitigating the effects and preventing sudden death.) Tj
T*
(TREATMENT:) Tj
T*
(* Request police assistance immediately.) Tj
T*
(* Initiate General Patient Care.) Tj
T*
(* Presentation:) Tj
T*
(Identify possible Hyper-Agitated Delirium using acronym PRIORITY. Presence of) Tj
T*
(some or all of these symptoms is indicative of potential syndrome.) Tj
T*
(a. P: Psychological issues) Tj
T*
(b. R: Recent drug/alcohol use) Tj
T*
(c. I: Incoherent thought processes) Tj
T*
(d. O: Off \(taking clothes off\) and sweating, HYPERTHERMIA) Tj
T*
(e. R: Resistant to presence or dialogue) Tj
T*
(f. I: Inanimate objects: violent toward shiny or glass objects) Tj
T*
(g. T: Tough, unstoppable, superhuman strength) Tj
T*
(h. Y: Yelling) Tj
T*
(* Providers should ensure crew safety at all times. \(See Restraint) Tj
T*
(Protocol\)) Tj
T*
(* Consider Ketamine 3-5 mg/kg IM. Maximum 500 mg. Contact Medical Control for) Tj
T*
(further doses.) Tj
T*
(* Consider Midazolam "Versed") Tj
T*
(a. 5-10 mg IM/IN) Tj
T*
(b. 5-10 mg IV, 2 mg increments) Tj
T*
(c. 0.1 mg/kg IV \(Pediatric dose\)) Tj
T*
(d. Maximum total dosing is 10 mg, call med control for additional) Tj
T*
(* Establish IV access after sedation, if not already established.) Tj
T*
(a. Infuse 1L of cool \(room temp, not from a warmer\) Normal Saline) Tj
T*
(b. Apply capnography to monitor patient respiratory status.) Tj
T*
(* Prepare to aggressively manage the airway if needed.) Tj
T*
(* Rapid Transport to the closest appropriate hospital with Medic and rider to) Tj
T*
(assist.) Tj
T*
(Sudden Death Factors) Tj
T*
(* Metabolic Acidosis) Tj
T*
(- Potentially life threatening abnormality of the blood chemistry) Tj
T*
(- Aggravated by:) Tj
T*
(* Increased activity, violent confrontation, dehydration) Tj
T*
(* Blood acidity affects vital functions) Tj
T*
(* Elevated blood potassium level) Tj
T*
(- Survivors) Tj
T*
(* Kidney damage due to muscle breakdown) Tj
T*
(* May require dialysis) Tj
