T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(NEEDLE / SURGICAL CRICOTHYROTOMY AIRWAY) Tj
T*
(PROCEDURE) Tj
T*
(Indications) Tj
T*
(1. Upper airway obstruction that is not relieved by BLS measures or direct) Tj
T*
(laryngoscopy with removal of object by magill forceps.) Tj
T*
(2. Severe facial trauma, which makes obtaining an airway by less invasive) Tj
T*
(means impossible.) Tj
T*
(Contraindications) Tj
T*
(1. Neck swelling that obscures landmarks.) Tj
T*
(2. Not a prophylactic measure. Must actually need an airway and ventilation) Tj
T*
(now.) Tj
T*
(Precautions) Tj
T*
(1. Contact medical control after procedure.) Tj
T*
(Technique) Tj
T*
(1. Locate the cricothyroid membrane between the thyroid and cricoid) Tj
T*
(cartilage.) Tj
T*
(2. Cleanse the area with betadine or alcohol as time permits.) Tj
T*
(3. Using the scalpel provided in the kit, make a 2 cm vertical incision over) Tj
T*
(the cricothyroid membrane.) Tj
T*
(4. Separate the incision and locate the cricothyroid membrane.) Tj
T*
(5. Using the scalpel, make an incision through the cricothyroid membrane.) Tj
T*
(6. Insert the dilator and tube into the trachea.) Tj
T*
(7. Remove the dilator and inflate the cuff of the tube.) Tj
T*
(8. Control any bleeding and apply sterile dressing around area of the) Tj
T*
(incision.) Tj
T*
(Complications) Tj
T*
(1. Placement at the wrong level can cause laryngeal or tracheal damage.) Tj
T*
(2. Bleeding) Tj
T*
(3. Massive subcutaneous and/or mediastinal emphysema) Tj
T*
(4. Pneumothorax) Tj
T*
ET
