(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(PLEURAL DECOMPRESSION) Tj
T*
(PLACE OCCLUSIVE DRESSING) Tj
T*
(Indications) Tj
T*
(Tension pneumothorax should be considered when the following) Tj
T*
(signs/symptoms are present:) Tj
T*
(1. Progressive severe respiratory distress.) Tj
T*
(2. Decreased or absent breath sounds on affected side.) Tj
T*
(3. Jugular vein distension.) Tj
T*
(4. Tracheal deviation away from the affected side.) Tj
T*
(5. Tympany to percussion on the affected side.) Tj
T*
(6. Cardiac compromise.) Tj
T*
(Contraindications) Tj
T*
(1. Not sure of diagnosis.) Tj
T*
(2. Clinical signs suggestive of diagnosis, but patient is not in shock and/or) Tj
T*
(respiratory distress.) Tj
T*
(Precautions) Tj
T*
(1. Contact medical control after procedure.) Tj
T*
(Technique) Tj
T*
(1. Locate the second and third intercostal space in the mid-clavicular line on) Tj
T*
(the affected side of the chest, or the fifth and sixth intercostal space in the) Tj
T*
(anterior-axillary line.) Tj
T*
(2. Cleanse with betadine or alcohol preps as time allows.) Tj
T*
(3. Insert a 14-guage catheter on the superior plane of the rib. Withdraw the) Tj
T*
(needle and attach a flutter valve to the catheter. Secure catheter to the) Tj
T*
(chest.) Tj
T*
(4. Re-evaluate respiratory status and vital signs.) Tj
T*
(Complications) Tj
T*
(1. Creation of a pneumothorax if one is not present.) Tj
T*
(2. Damage to lung or viscera.) Tj
T*
(3. Bleeding \(intercostal vessels are below each rib\).) Tj
T*
(4. Infection) Tj
T*
ET
