T*
(CAPNOGRAPHY) Tj
T*
(Clinical Indications:) Tj
T*
(Capnography shall be used when available with the use of all invasive airway procedures) Tj
T*
(including but not limited to endotracheal intubation, nasotracheal intubation,) Tj
T*
(cricothyrotomy,) Tj
T*
(or Blind Insertion Airway Devices \(BIAD\). Capnography shall also be used: In accordance) Tj
T*
(with current ACLS recommendations for determining effectiveness of resuscitation efforts) Tj
T*
(\(10 mm/Hg or above\), on all patients in respiratory distress, and all patients undergoing) Tj
T*
(sedation.) Tj
T*
(Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Attach capnography sensors.) Tj
T*
(2. Note CO2 level and waveform changes. These will be documented on each respiratory) Tj
T*
(failure, cardiac arrest, or severe respiratory distress patient.) Tj
T*
(3. The capnometer shall remain in place with the airway and be monitored throughout the) Tj
T*
(prehospital care and transport.) Tj
T*
(4. Any loss of CO2 detection or waveform indicates an airway problem or device malfunction) Tj
T*
(and should be documented.) Tj
T*
(5. The capnogram should be monitored as procedures are performed to verify or correct the) Tj
T*
(airway problem.) Tj
T*
(6. Document the procedure and results on/with the Patient Care Report \(PCR\).) Tj
T*
ET
