T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(SPINAL CLEARANCE) Tj
T*
(Indications:) Tj
T*
(To allow Paramedics to perform field clearance from full spinal) Tj
T*
(restrictions.) Tj
T*
(Contraindications) Tj
T*
(1. Any patient less than 12 years of age) Tj
T*
(2. Patients with chronic neck or back pain) Tj
T*
(3. Patients exhibiting signs of shock) Tj
T*
(4. Signs/symptoms of alcohol or drug intoxication) Tj
T*
(5. Altered Mental Status) Tj
T*
(6. Distracting Injuries) Tj
T*
(-Full spinal precautions must take place if yes was answered to any of the) Tj
T*
(above questions.) Tj
T*
(*Maintain a high index of suspicion with older/elderly patients, as occult) Tj
T*
(fractures are possible with benign mechanisms of injury or trauma.) Tj
T*
(-If the patient meets the criteria to withhold spinal precautions, EMS providers) Tj
T*
(may still elect to provide spinal precautions.) Tj
T*
(Examples of distracting) Tj
T*
(injuries:) Tj
T*
(Extremity fractures, rib) Tj
T*
(fractures, pelvic fractures,) Tj
T*
(abdominal pain from trauma) Tj
T*
(related injury, and other) Tj
T*
(significant injuries.) Tj
T*
(Assessment) Tj
T*
(All patients will be assessed by the following criteria. Only those of) Tj
T*
(whom answer no to all requirements, may be cleared.) Tj
T*
(1. Does the patient have a GCS less than 15?) Tj
T*
(2. Does the patient complain of neck or back pain?) Tj
T*
(3. Is there tenderness, swelling, or deformity noted when the) Tj
T*
(complete spine is palpated? You must visualize and palpate the) Tj
T*
(entire spine: neck to lower lumbar.) Tj
T*
(4. Is there a distracting injury or distracting pain?) Tj
T*
(5. Are there signs/symptoms of alcohol or drug intoxication present?) Tj
T*
(Examples of) Tj
T*
(signs/symptoms of) Tj
T*
(intoxication:) Tj
T*
(GCS <15, slurred speech,) Tj
T*
(dilated/constricted pupils,) Tj
T*
(flushed skin, unsteady gate,) Tj
T*
(irregular behavior, presence of) Tj
T*
(paraphernalia or admitted use.) Tj
T*
ET
