T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(VITAL SIGNS) Tj
T*
(INDICATIONS:) Tj
T*
(1. A minimum of two sets of vitals will be obtained on every transported patient.) Tj
T*
(This will include Pulse, Respirations, BP, Spo2 and alert and oriented status.) Tj
T*
(2. A minimum of one set of vitals will be taken on refusals.) Tj
T*
(Technique:) Tj
T*
(1. The first set of vitals a manual blood pressure and pulse will be taken on the) Tj
T*
(following calls: chest pain, stroke, overdose, syncope, trauma, hypo/) Tj
T*
(hypertension, anaphylaxis and any unconscious or critical patient.) Tj
T*
(2. A manual BP will be taken if the automated device is more than 30 points) Tj
T*
(different than first set obtained \(systolic or diastolic\) in either direction.) Tj
T*
(3. A full set of vitals will be taken after each medication administration.) Tj
T*
(4. Capillary refill and/or an automated blood pressure device is expectable for) Tj
T*
(pediatric patients.) Tj
T*
(ORTHOSTATIC VITAL SIGNS) Tj
T*
(Indications:) Tj
T*
(1. Syncope or Near Syncope \(ie. dizzy, faint\)) Tj
T*
(TECHNIQUE:) Tj
T*
(Patient in supine position for minimum of three minutes before taking lying blood pressure) Tj
T*
(and pulse, then stand) Tj
T*
(patient and immediately repeat blood pressure and pulse. If patient unable to stand, sit him) Tj
T*
(upright with legs) Tj
T*
(dangling over cot.) Tj
T*
(SPECIAL NOTES AND EVALUATION:) Tj
T*
(1. Orthostatic changes are not valid if:) Tj
T*
(a. Taken initially upright, then supine.) Tj
T*
(b. Taken upright with only head of cot elevated and legs not dangling.) Tj
T*
(c. If only pulse or blood pressure is checked by itself. Must have both blood) Tj
T*
(pressure and pulses in both positions.) Tj
T*
(2. Significant orthostatic changes include:) Tj
T*
(a. Pulse increase greater than 20 beats per minute when moved upright.) Tj
T*
(b. Pressure \(diastolic most significant\) drop greater than 20 MM Hg when) Tj
T*
(upright.) Tj
T*
(c. Pallor, diaphoresis, or faintness when upright.) Tj
T*
(3. Significant changes could indicate volume depletion \(dehydration or blood loss\),) Tj
T*
(treat the symptoms, follow DEHYDRATION protocol if indicated.) Tj
T*
(4. Considerations:) Tj
T*
(a. Treat the symptoms.) Tj
T*
(b. Medications can often cause changes, usually indicated by pressure) Tj
T*
(change but no pulse change.) Tj
T*
(c. May be due to slowing of compensatory mechanisms in the elderly.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
