T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(ALBUTEROL & ATROVENT \(Duoneb\)) Tj
T*
(PHARMACOLOGY & ACTIONS:) Tj
T*
(A potent relatively selective beta 2 - adrenergic bronchodilator.) Tj
T*
(Has occasional beta 1 overlap with clinically significant cardiac effects.) Tj
T*
(INDICATIONS:) Tj
T*
(Bronchial asthma) Tj
T*
(Reversible bronchial spasm that occurs with chronic pulmonary disease.) Tj
T*
(CONTRAINDICATIONS:) Tj
T*
(Stop treatment if pulse increases by 20 bpm, frequent PVC's develop, any) Tj
T*
(tachyarrhythmias other than sinus tachycardia appear, chest pain, apnea,) Tj
T*
(nausea or vomiting, or increased shortness of breath occur.) Tj
T*
(Patients with allergies to soy or peanuts should not be administered) Tj
T*
(Atrovent) Tj
T*
(ADMINISTRATION:) Tj
T*
(Nebulizer dosage for adults & children over 1 year - 2.5 mg mixed in 3 ml of) Tj
T*
(saline for a concentration of .83 mg/ml.) Tj
T*
(Infants under 1 year: Nebulizer dosage 0.03 ml/kg max dose 1ml.) Tj
T*
(Nebulization:) Tj
T*
(Oxygen flow should be set at 6 Lpm.) Tj
T*
(Patients should inhale slowly & exhale passively through nose.) Tj
T*
(SIDE EFFECTS & SPECIAL NOTES:) Tj
T*
(Patients with COPD should be monitored carefully for CO2 retention & decreased) Tj
T*
(levels of consciousness.) Tj
T*
(Paradoxical bronchospasm may occur with excessive administration.) Tj
T*
(Skeletal muscle tremors) Tj
T*
(Albuterol should be used with caution in pregnancy.) Tj
T*
(Continually assess patient's respiratory rate, effort, and lung sounds.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
