BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 104 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(DILTIAZEM HCL \(CARDIZEM\)) Tj
T*
(CLASS OF DRUG) Tj
T*
(Calcium Channel Blocker; Coronary Vasodilator, Antidysrhythmic) Tj
T*
(INDICATIONS) Tj
T*
(1. Symptomatic Atrial Fibrillation or Atrial Flutter with rapid ventricular response) Tj
T*
(2. Symptomatic Paroxysmal Supraventricular Tachycardia) Tj
T*
(CONTRAINDICATIONS) Tj
T*
(1. Sick sinus syndrome except in the presence of a functioning ventricular) Tj
T*
(pacemaker.) Tj
T*
(2. Patients with second- or third degree AV block except in the presence of) Tj
T*
(a functioning ventricular pacemaker.) Tj
T*
(3. Patients with severe hypotension, cardiogenic shock or severe CHF) Tj
T*
(4. Patients who have demonstrated hypersensitivity to the drug) Tj
T*
(5. Patients with atrial fibrillation or atrial flutter associated with an accessory) Tj
T*
(bypass tract such as in WPW syndrome or short PR syndrome) Tj
T*
(6. Patients with ventricular tachycardia) Tj
T*
(7. Pregnancy) Tj
T*
(8. Children under the age of 15) Tj
T*
(WARNING- DILTIAZEM use in severe congestive heart failure; patients with reduced) Tj
T*
(ventricular function may not be able to counteract the inotropic and chronotropic effects of) Tj
T*
(diltiazem, the result being an even higher compromise of function.) Tj
T*
(DRUG INTERACTION) Tj
T*
(Additive effects in prolonging AV conduction when using beta-blockers or) Tj
T*
(digitalis concomitantly with Diltiazem HCl.) Tj
T*
(ADMINISTRATION \(For patients over age 70 decrease dose by 5mg\)) Tj
T*
(0.25 mg/kg max 20mg SIVP over 2 minutes, continue to monitor the PT, if hypotension) Tj
T*
(develops, DC medication and consider a fluid bolus. Repeat 12 lead ECG if rhythm) Tj
T*
(converts. If no response after 10 minutes, consider a second dose of 0.35mg/kg max) Tj
T*
(20mg SIVP over 2 minutes. If hypotension develops DC medication and consider a fluid) Tj
T*
(bolus. Repeat 12 lead ECG if the rhythm converts.) Tj
T*
(SPECIAL NOTES) Tj
T*
(*Pediatric: Not usually used.) Tj
T*
(*DO NOT TREAT BRADYCARDIA WITH ATROPINE, DILTIAZEM WILL WEAR OFF.) Tj
T*
(*For patients over age 70 decrease dose by 5mg.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
