T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(ZOFRAN \(ONDANSETRON\)) Tj
T*
(Classification:) Tj
T*
(Anitemetic) Tj
T*
(Actions/Pharmacology:) Tj
T*
(Blocks the effects of serotonin at 5-HT3 receptor sites \(selective antagonist\) located in) Tj
T*
(vagal) Tj
T*
(nerve terminals and the chemoreceptor trigger zone in the CNS.) Tj
T*
(Indications:) Tj
T*
(Nausea and vomiting, regardless of mechanism.) Tj
T*
(Contraindications:) Tj
T*
(Age < 4 years) Tj
T*
(Parkinson's patients receiving Apomorphine) Tj
T*
(Side and Adverse effects:) Tj
T*
(Headache) Tj
T*
(Sedation) Tj
T*
(Constipation) Tj
T*
(Diarrhea) Tj
T*
(Transient blindness) Tj
T*
(May cause transient dizziness after IV administration) Tj
T*
(May cause prolonged QT interval and/or Torsade de Pointes) Tj
T*
(May cause transient oculogyric crisis and dystonic reactions) Tj
T*
(Adult Administration:) Tj
T*
(4mg IM or orally dissolving tablet \(ODT\)) Tj
T*
(4mg slow IVP over 2 to 5 minutes) Tj
T*
(Must contact medical control for additional doses.) Tj
T*
(Pediatric Administration:) Tj
T*
(Must be 4 years of age and older) Tj
T*
(2mg IM or ODT) Tj
T*
(2mg slow IVP over 2 to 5 minutes) Tj
T*
(Must contact medical control for additional doses.) Tj
T*
(Interactions:) Tj
T*
(When taken with apomorphine, may cause hypotension and ALOC) Tj
T*
(Precautions:) Tj
T*
(Tablet should not be handled with moist or wet hands) Tj
T*
(May cause prolonged QT interval and/or Torsade de Pointes) Tj
T*
(Patients receiving IV administration should be placed on cardiac monitor) Tj
T*
(Special Considerations:) Tj
T*
(Tablet should be placed onto tongue and allowed to dissolve.) Tj
T*
