269 0 obj
<< /Length 2652 >>
stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 133 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(TPOPP for EMS) Tj
T*
(What is TPOPP?) Tj
T*
(Transportable Physician Orders for Patient Preferences \(TPOPP\) is a program) Tj
T*
(designed to improve the quality of care people receive at the end of life by translating) Tj
T*
(patient/resident goals and preferences into medical orders for treatment.) Tj
T*
(What is the TPOPP form?) Tj
T*
(The TPOPP form is a bright pink piece of paper that can communicate patient) Tj
T*
(preferences regarding life-sustaining medical treatment. When signed by a patient \(or a) Tj
T*
(recognized decision maker\) and a physician licensed in Kansas or Missouri, it becomes) Tj
T*
(a medical order. Providers at all sites of care should follow the medical orders.) Tj
T*
(What types of medical orders are on the form?) Tj
T*
(The form includes medical orders and patient preferences regarding:) Tj
T*
(CPR) Tj
T*
(Implementing comfort care) Tj
T*
(Defibrillation and cardioversion) Tj
T*
(Intubation and mechanical ventilation) Tj
T*
(Transport decisions) Tj
T*
(Who might have a TPOPP form?) Tj
T*
(TPOPP is designed for persons who have advanced progressive chronic illness or are) Tj
T*
(terminally ill. EMS may see TPOPP forms for persons who:) Tj
T*
(Live independently;) Tj
T*
(Reside in a long-term care or assisted living facility;) Tj
T*
(Receive hospice care.) Tj
T*
(Does every person with advanced chronic or terminal illness have a form?) Tj
T*
(No. TPOPP is voluntary and based on the belief that an individual has the right to make) Tj
T*
(his or her own health care decisions. TPOPP forms can be used by persons of any age) Tj
T*
(with an advanced progressive illness or who is terminally ill.) Tj
T*
(How is a TPOPP form completed?) Tj
T*
(The TPOPP form is completed after having a conversation with the patient \(or) Tj
T*
(recognized decision maker\) and a member of the healthcare team such as a physician,) Tj
T*
(nurse, social worker or chaplain. When the patient \(or recognized decision maker\) and a) Tj
T*
(physician sign the form it is complete. Both signatures are necessary. The signatures) Tj
T*
(verify that the preferences on the form are consistent with the patient's values and) Tj
T*
(treatment goals.) Tj
T*
(What do you do with a completed form?) Tj
T*
(The TPOPP form travels with the patient between care settings. The original form) Tj
T*
(should accompany the patient and be presented to each provider \(first responder,) Tj
T*
(hospital or other care setting\).) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
270 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 271 0 R >>
endobj
271 0 obj
<< /Length 3331 >>
stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 134 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(Where is the form kept?) Tj
T*
(EMS personnel should look for or ask for the form. It should be conspicuously located:) Tj
T*
(In the front of the patient's medical chart at care facilities;) Tj
T*
(On the refrigerator, by a phone, or bedside when the patient resides at home;) Tj
T*
(The TPOPP form should go with the patient when the person is transferred from the) Tj
T*
(hospital or health care setting.) Tj
T*
(How is the form used by EMS?) Tj
T*
(EMS should administer the level of treatment ordered in Section A and in Section B) Tj
T*
(when they arrive on scene. EMS will transfer the individual to the emergency room if) Tj
T*
(ordered or contact medical control for further instructions.) Tj
T*
(What sections apply to EMS providers?) Tj
T*
(Section A orders apply only when the person is in cardiopulmonary arrest. If the) Tj
T*
("Attempt Resuscitation/CPR" box is checked then CPR should be performed. If the "Do) Tj
T*
(Not Attempt Resuscitation \(DNAR/no CPR/Allow Natural Death\)" box is checked, CPR) Tj
T*
(should not be performed. Comfort measures are provided and CPR is not attempted.) Tj
T*
(Section B orders apply to emergency medical circumstances for a person who has a) Tj
T*
(pulse and/or is breathing. These range from full treatment to comfort measures only. If) Tj
T*
(all life-sustaining treatments are desired the "Full Treatment" box is checked. However,) Tj
T*
(if the person desires some limitation, then either the "Comfort Measures Only" box or) Tj
T*
(the "Limited Additional Interventions" box is checked. EMS first will administer the level) Tj
T*
(of emergency medical services ordered and then contact medical control as needed.) Tj
T*
(Comfort care is always provided regardless of indicated level of EMS treatment.) Tj
T*
(If Attempt Resuscitation in Section A is checked, then Full Treatment in Section B is) Tj
T*
(checked. Full resuscitation implies full treatment. Section D validates the order with the) Tj
T*
(dated signatures of the physician and patient \(or recognized decision maker\).) Tj
T*
(When can EMS honor the TPOPP form?) Tj
T*
(EMS personnel can honor the TPOPP form in any situation in which a valid TPOPP) Tj
T*
(form is presented for the patient requiring emergency medical care.) Tj
T*
(Will the person still have or need a signed Outside the Hospital Do Not) Tj
T*
(resuscitate \(DNR\) form?) Tj
T*
(Your organization/agency will determine the specific policies associated with TPOPP.) Tj
T*
(Remember, that if DNAR is selected in Section A and the form is valid, you have a) Tj
T*
(physician's order not to resuscitate.) Tj
T*
(Is a copy or faxed copy of the form acceptable?) Tj
T*
(Yes - A copy, faxed copy, or electronic representation of the TPOPP form is acceptable) Tj
T*
(provided it has the person's name and signatures of the physician and patient \(or) Tj
T*
(recognized decision maker\).) Tj
T*
(Where can I get more information?) Tj
T*
(Visit the website of the Center for Practical Bioethics at www.practicalbioethics.org,) Tj
T*
(send an e-mail to TPOPP@practicalbioethics.org or call the TPOPP Managing Director at) Tj
T*
(816-979-1366.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
