275 0 obj
<< /Length 1846 >>
stream
BT
/F1 9 Tf
11 TL
40 760 Td
(Gladstone Fire Department EMS Protocols - 2026 Revision V3) Tj
T*
(Text-rendered internal source copy | Original PDF physical page 136 of 142) Tj
T*
T*
(05/23/2025) Tj
T*
(Apneic Oxygenation) Tj
T*
(Prior to intubation apply a nasal cannula and flow at 8-10 LPM) Tj
T*
(In an experiment by Frumin et al., patients were pre-oxygenated, intubated, paralyzed, and) Tj
T*
(placed on an anesthesia machine that provided 1.0 fiO2 and no ventilations. These patients) Tj
T*
(were maintained in this apneic state for between 18 and 55 min. none of these patients) Tj
T*
(desaturated below 98%, despite being paralyzed and receiving no breaths. Although their) Tj
T*
(CO2 levels rose, their oxygenation was maintained due to apneic oxygenation. Oxygen was) Tj
T*
(absorbed from the patients' alveoli by pulmonary blood flow; this established a gradient for) Tj
T*
(the continued pull of oxygen from the endotracheal tube and anesthesia circuit. In another) Tj
T*
(study, Teller et al. showed that pharyngeal insufflation with oxygen significantly extended) Tj
T*
(the) Tj
T*
(time to desaturation during apnea.) Tj
T*
(Numerous studies on apneic oxygenation during brain death testing confirm that even) Tj
T*
(without any respiratory effort, oxygen saturation can be maintained. If a continuous path of) Tj
T*
(oxygen is maintained from the pharynx to the glottis during the apneic period of RSI, the) Tj
T*
(patient will continue to oxygenate. This has led us to perform a jaw thrust in all high-risk) Tj
T*
(patients during their apneic period. In some cases, we also place nasopharyngeal airways to) Tj
T*
(augment the passage of oxygen. These techniques, combined with high-flow O2 from a) Tj
T*
(High flow cannula, NRB mask, NIV mask, or the facemask of a BVM, will allow continued) Tj
T*
(apneic oxygenation.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
276 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R >> >> /Contents 277 0 R >>
